# ============================================================
# .gitignore for Universal AI Dialogue Logger
# ============================================================
# Purpose:
#   This file prevents demo/test artifacts from being
#   accidentally committed to the repository.
#
#   When you run `python demo_usage.py`, the DialogueLogger
#   auto-generates a SQLite database and Markdown logs in the
#   current working directory. These are runtime outputs, not
#   source code — they should NOT be version-controlled.
#
# If you DO want to commit your logs or database:
#   1. Remove the corresponding line below.
#   2. Run: git add -f <filename>
#      (The -f flag forces Git to track an ignored file.)
#   3. Commit as usual: git commit -m "Add my conversation data"
#
# Example:
#   git add -f my_memory.db
#   git add -f Formatted_Logs/
# ============================================================

# --- SQLite database files (auto-generated at runtime) ---
*.db

# --- Markdown export directories (auto-generated by auto-flush) ---
Formatted_Logs/
Demo_Logs/

# --- Python cache ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
